## 15. COMMITMENT TRACKING

Display purchase commitments from actual Purchase Order records.

Important business rule:

A Purchase Requisition does not create a commitment.

Cost Committed arises only when a Purchase Order is approved.

Use this proposed calculation:

Cost Committed (open) = Approved PO Value − Posted Invoice Value against that PO.

Minimum value: zero.

Label this calculation:

"Proposed – pending client validation".

Do not generate fictional purchase commitments.

Until Procurement is implemented, show an appropriate empty state or zero based on the available records.

## 16. ACTUAL COST TRACKING

Display actual project expenditure derived from posted supplier invoices.

Use this proposed rule:

Cost Incurred = Posted supplier invoices tagged to the project and cost code.

Important distinctions:

- Uploaded invoices are not actual costs.
- AI-extracted invoices are not actual costs.
- Unverified invoices are not actual costs.
- Only posted invoices contribute to Cost Incurred.

Display actual costs by project, C-Code and S-Code wherever the transaction data supports this.

Do not double-count material purchases through both invoices and material issues.

Label this calculation:

"Proposed – pending client validation".

Until Finance is implemented, show an appropriate empty state or zero based on the available records.

## 17. BUDGET VS. COMMITMENT

Compare the approved budget with open purchase commitments.

